Keep a multisampled window surface's samples on the GPU's tiles only (Minato, patch 0016).

Why: an EGL window surface with EGL_SAMPLES 4 got a multisample color texture in private memory, four times the
window's size (55 MiB at 1290 x 2796), on top of the drawable it resolves into. An Android tiler keeps an EGL
surface's samples in its tile memory and writes only the resolved frame. On Apple GPUs a memoryless texture does
the same: when ANGLE resolves at the end of each render pass (allowMultisampleStoreAndResolve), the window's
multisample color is memoryless, and a render pass that loads gets the resolved color back into its samples, as
FramebufferMtl::unresolveIfNeeded already does for EXT_multisampled_render_to_texture.
Test: graphics/tests/angle_window_msaa.mm (a 4x window keeps what a frame drew before it left the window for a
framebuffer object and came back, and patch 0015's counters show its multisample color as memoryless).
Upstream: could go upstream.
diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/SurfaceMtl.mm b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/SurfaceMtl.mm
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/SurfaceMtl.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/SurfaceMtl.mm
@@ -346,9 +346,21 @@
     {
         mAutoResolveMSColorTexture =
             contextMtl->getDisplay()->getFeatures().allowMultisampleStoreAndResolve.enabled;
-        ANGLE_TRY(CreateOrResizeTexture(context, mColorFormat, size.width, size.height, mSamples,
-                                        /** renderTargetOnly */ mAutoResolveMSColorTexture,
-                                        &mMSColorTexture));
+        if (mAutoResolveMSColorTexture)
+        {
+            // Minato (patch 0016): the samples live on the GPU's tiles only, as an Android tiler keeps an
+            // EGL surface's; each render pass resolves into the drawable, and one that loads gets the
+            // resolved color back into its samples (FramebufferMtl::unresolveIfNeeded).
+            mMSColorTexture = nullptr;
+            ANGLE_TRY(mtl::Texture::MakeMemoryLess2DMSTexture(contextMtl, mColorFormat, size.width,
+                                                              size.height, mSamples,
+                                                              &mMSColorTexture));
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            ANGLE_TRY(CreateOrResizeTexture(context, mColorFormat, size.width, size.height, mSamples,
+                                            /** renderTargetOnly */ false, &mMSColorTexture));
+        }
 
         if (mAutoResolveMSColorTexture)
         {
